# Functions as values

## Behaviour becomes a value

The anonymous class from module 02…

```java
button.addListener(new ClickListener() {
    @Override public void onClick() { System.out.println("clicked"); }
});
```

…is just a lambda — a **function literal**:

```java
button.addListener(() -> System.out.println("clicked"));
```

## What makes it work

A lambda's type is a **functional interface** — exactly **one abstract method** (a SAM). The lambda supplies that method's body.

```java
Comparator<String> byLength = (a, b) -> a.length() - b.length();
Runnable greet              = () -> System.out.println("hi");
```

## Why it matters

- **Parameterise behaviour** — `list.sort(byLength)` passes the *rule*
- **Callbacks** as one-liners; **small pieces compose** → streams (module 07)

**The one idea:** a function is a value — do with behaviour what you do with data.
